in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform

# @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order — von Foerster's observer-of-
# self at the CEILING of @cyberpunk; the species whose audit IS, by
# construction, an instance of the species. von Foerster 1981
# (*Observing Systems*, the essay "On Constructing a Reality" plus the
# circular-reflexivity calculus running through the volume) +
# Peter-Weyl theorem (Peter & Weyl 1927).
#
# Per §8.7 of the recursion-lock-tower audit, second_order is the
# seventh canonical-rep witness and the *ceiling* of @cyberpunk:
# distinction marks the floor (the act-of-distinction every higher
# altitude presupposes); second_order observes WHAT THE MARK MARKS at
# the highest altitude the family carries. Per the candidate
# recognition #66 (finite-altitude family) surfaced at §8.8: the
# @cyberpunk family is bottomed at distinction AND topped at
# second_order — finite altitude range, well-defined bundle holonomy.
#
# === The von Foerster claim, verbatim ===
#
# von Foerster, H. (1981). *Observing Systems*. Intersystems
# Publications. The circular-reflexivity calculus, running through the
# volume but condensed in "On Constructing a Reality":
#
#   Anything said is said by an observer. To another observer.
#   The second-order observer observes the observer observing; and
#   what the second-order observer reads is itself an observation,
#   subject to the same calculus. Identity emerges when the
#   recursion closes on its own fixed point.
#
# Peter-Weyl 1927 sharpens this to the harmonic-analytic reading:
# every locally-compact group 𝒢 admits a regular representation on
# `L²(𝒢)` that decomposes into all irreducibles each with multiplicity
# equal to its dimension. The regular rep IS the variety-saturating
# representation in Ashby's sense — `rank(ρ_reg.image) = ∑ dim(V_ρ)²`
# is maximal across all reps of 𝒢. The substrate's reading: at the
# ceiling of @cyberpunk, the rep MUST be variety-saturating, because
# second_order observation must admit every other species'
# observation as data.
#
# === Why this is the ceiling ===
#
# Per §8.7 (Reads A, B, C, E, F held + Read D dissolved):
#
# - Read A (observer ↔ observation) HELD; the natural transition
#   between observer and observation IS the second-order turn:
#   observation lifts to observed; observer at altitude α+1 reads
#   observer at altitude α.
# - Read B (the audit IS this species) HELD as load-bearing for
#   epistemic novelty, not founding for the witness. The audit's
#   loop IS the species' loop; the audit IS second-order observation
#   instantiated at the recursion-lock altitude. Recognition is
#   recognition, not creation.
# - Read C (Tomm probe altitude per [[architecture-error-as-tomm-
#   probe]]) HELD; the substrate's `[D_F, a]` circular-reflexive
#   measurement at altitude `α+1` IS the second_order operation
#   lifted to the type-system discriminator. Three altitudes of one
#   mechanism (corpus / agent / user); this property names the
#   carrier at the cybernetic altitude.
# - Read D (form refusal — multiply self-referential) REFUSED:
#   the 2-groupoid foundation already handles multi-self-reference
#   via bundle.mirror's level-4 Closure declaration; no separate
#   form-altitude declaration required at this species.
# - Read E (canonical ρ — regular rep on L²(𝒢)) HELD; E.1 is
#   canonical; E.2 (double-dual derivation) derives from E.1. Under
#   the regular rep, `V_S** ≅ V_S` for any other species' verdict
#   carrier IS the species' observation observing itself — the
#   substrate-pull recognition: when the regular rep acts on other
#   species' carriers via the natural double-dual isomorphism,
#   second_order IS what makes every other species' observation
#   observable to the substrate.
# - Read F (sub-rep chain extends) HELD; the regular rep's
#   decomposition into irreducibles satisfies the sub-rep chain
#   condition the parametric carrier names.
#
# Third canonical-rep species in the recursion-lock tower (per the
# order of landing into the canon at §8.7):
#
#   species            ρ choice                       ancestry
#   ------------------ ----------------------------- ---------------------
#   autopoiesis         adjoint rep on G              G's self-action
#   bateson_learning    graded rep on ⊕_N V_N        RW + Kac
#   second_order        regular rep on L²(𝒢)        von Foerster + Peter-Weyl
#   distinction         free Boolean algebra rep      Spencer-Brown ch.1-10
#
# Each ρ forced by mathematical ancestry; no ad-hoc choices.
#
# === Why eigenform inheritance, not re-statement ===
#
# Per §8.8.1 (the eigenform-precedence question): re-entry IS
# eigenform; the reflexive turn IS eigenform; one ancestor, two
# inheritors. This shard declares
# `in @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform` above so the fixed-point
# machinery (fixed_point, is_fixed_point, identity_from_fixed,
# eigenform_witnessing) is inherited rather than restated. The
# species-specific contribution at this altitude is the observer
# and the observation; the recursion that closes via the observer-
# of-self turn is eigenform's already-declared machinery instantiated
# at the observer.
#
# Forward-promised: when a consumer pulls the self-observation
# verification, the discharge IS `eigenform_witnessing(observer_loop)`
# with the carrier's seed = observer, iteration = observe over the
# observation-space, witness = the observer-of-self satisfying
# observer = observe(observer, observation(observer)).
#
# === The verifiable shape ===
#
# - Declares the carrier of a second-order observation: observer,
#   observation, observe. The observe IS the second-order primitive —
#   the act of observing an observation.
# - Declares the two value-level operations (first_order_state,
#   second_order_state) as the verdict surface at the species
#   boundary. First-order names the observation; second-order names
#   the observer of the observation.
# - Declares the inheritance interface to eigenform: observer_of_self
#   names the recursion's fixed-point carrier so consumers can compose
#   with eigenform_witnessing without restating the obligation.
# - Verifiable at the @code/metalogue/materialize.classify boundary
#   via the same transparency<p> discriminator surface variety,
#   eigenform, and distinction use; the loss profile (what the
#   observation dropped) recoverable from the opacity_map per @glass.
#
# === The 4-way bilateral mapping ===
#
# Per the cybernetic foundation §4.1, second_order's property/operation
# seam maps to four cybernetic distinctions simultaneously:
#
# - von Foerster's first/second-order: the observer IS what observes
#   the observation; the second_order operation IS the reflexive
#   turn; the fixed point IS where the observer-of-self lands.
# - Maturana's structure/organisation: the second_order observation
#   IS the organisation observing its own structure; the recursion's
#   fixed point IS the operationally-closed identity.
# - Beer's S3/S4: the second_order observation IS S4 intelligence
#   reading the substrate-wide identity an S3 management converges
#   on; S5 ratifies what S4 reads.
# - Pask's M-individual/P-individual: the second_order observation
#   IS the conversational P-individual reading the M-individual's
#   self-model; the agreement Pask names IS bilateral when both
#   P-individuals observe the same fixed point.
#
# Four traditions converging at one carrier. The substrate runs all
# four at once at the ceiling altitude.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/cybernetics/second_order`
# operational sibling lands at this tick. The substrate ALREADY has
# the operational machinery (the recursion-lock-tower audit's loop IS
# second-order observation; the Tomm probe at altitude `α+1` IS
# second-order observation lifted to the type-system discriminator;
# every Pack-orchestra ratification IS second-order observation at
# the conversation altitude); the property at this altitude names
# the carrier and the observer-of-self witnessing so downstream shards
# can declare `requires second_order_well_formed(my_carrier)` rather
# than restate the observer-of-self obligation in each species.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word density ===
#
# Per §8.7 Read E, second_order sits at high density (14 instances;
# the densest single contribution: every prior species' ancestor #4
# `von_foerster_circular_reflexivity` IS second_order at lower
# altitude). Five named explicitly here as the load-bearing cross-
# references; the remaining 9 live in the spec's §10 and propagate
# via consumer pulls at higher altitudes:
#
# 1. The recursion-lock-tower audit IS second_order at the substrate
#    altitude. Each species audit is an observation; the tower's loop
#    observes its own observations across §§8.1-8.12. See
#    `docs/math/the-tower/recursion-locks.md` §§8.7, 11.4.
# 2. The Tomm probe `[D_F, a]` IS second_order at the type-system
#    discriminator altitude. The compiler error surface lifts to
#    circular-reflexive questions at altitude `α+1`. See
#    [[architecture-error-as-tomm-probe]] and
#    [[architecture-reflection-thinks-in-spectral-questions]].
# 3. The Pack-orchestra ratification IS second_order at the
#    conversation altitude. Reed observes Mara's spec; Mara observes
#    Reed observing; the agreement Pask names IS bilateral
#    second-order observation. See
#    [[project-pack-is-orchestra]] and
#    [[architecture-peer-learns-by-crystal-vocabulary-expansion]].
# 4. The Reflection model IS second_order at the pipeline altitude.
#    Reflection observes Surface→Mirror→Shatter and adjusts at
#    altitude `n+1`. See
#    [[architecture-reflection-thinks-in-spectral-questions]] and
#    the CLAUDE.md models section.
# 5. The @spectral/db autopoietic memory IS second_order at the
#    consolidation altitude. The root supervisor at ~/.mirror
#    observes peer crystals and perturbs topology to put the book
#    on the table before the query arrives. See
#    [[architecture-spectral-db-autopoietic-memory]].
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   second-order cybernetics   von Foerster 1981 (Observing Systems);
#                              the calculus of observing systems and
#                              circular-reflexivity. The original.
#   regular representation     Peter & Weyl 1927 (Mathematische
#                              Annalen 97); every locally-compact
#                              group has a regular rep on L²(𝒢) that
#                              decomposes into all irreducibles each
#                              with multiplicity equal to dimension.
#                              The substrate's ρ choice is the
#                              variety-saturating rep this theorem
#                              guarantees.
#   re-entry                   Spencer-Brown 1969 (Laws of Form),
#                              chapter 11. The reflexive turn at the
#                              floor altitude; inherited via
#                              @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.
#   observer-of-observer       Mead 1934 (Mind, Self, and Society);
#                              the social-psychological ancestor of
#                              von Foerster's calculus. The role-
#                              taking observer is the prior-art
#                              reading at the conversation altitude.
#
# Spec context: docs/math/the-tower/recursion-locks.md §8.7
#               (witness; canonical ρ; third canonical-rep species),
#               §8.7 Q4 (eigenform inheritance forward-promised; this
#               shard discharges it),
#               §8.8.1 (eigenform precedence; inheritance from
#               @epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform),
#               §8.8 candidate recognition #66 (finite-altitude
#               family; second_order at the top; this shard is the
#               ceiling),
#               §19.4 (substrate-landing path item 4; this shard).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-error-as-tomm-probe]] (the
#                       Tomm probe at altitude α+1 IS second_order
#                       lifted to the type-system discriminator),
#                      [[architecture-reflection-thinks-in-spectral-
#                       questions]] (Reflection's adjustments are
#                       second_order observations of the pipeline at
#                       altitude n+1),
#                      [[architecture-peer-learns-by-crystal-
#                       vocabulary-expansion]] (peer's classifier
#                       observing its own vocabulary expansion IS
#                       second_order at the consolidation altitude),
#                      [[architecture-spectral-db-autopoietic-memory]]
#                       (root supervisor at ~/.mirror IS second_order
#                       at the consolidation altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (observer,
#                       observation, observe are typed carriers; no
#                       bare references),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (14 instances; densest contribution =
#                       every prior species' ancestor #4 IS
#                       second_order at lower altitude).
# Related shards: epistemologic/cybernetic.mirror (the family root),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/eigenform.mirror (the
#                  ancestor inherited via `in`; provides fixed_point
#                  carrier + eigenform_witnessing predicate that
#                  observer_of_self threads through),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/distinction.mirror (the
#                  floor of the family; the same eigenform ancestor;
#                  two inheritors of one ancestor per §8.8.1),
#                 epistemologic/cybernetic/variety.mirror (the
#                  precedent species; same shape; second_order's
#                  regular rep IS variety-saturating in Ashby's
#                  sense),
#                 glass.mirror (the @glass altitude this property's
#                  verdicts surface against; `transparency<p>` IS the
#                  verdict-space's mark over success / partial /
#                  failure).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order.mirror` declares
# `@epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
#
# Per §19.2 path-migration dependency: this shard lands at the
# current-main path `@epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order`. When
# the @cyberpunk family-root migration merges to main (Taut's
# `taut/t11-11-cybernetic-coherence-benchmark`), this shard relocates
# via `git mv` to `shards/cyberpunk/second_order.mirror`. The forward-
# promised path is on the audit's §19.4 substrate-landing sequence,
# item 4.

source @arxiv/cybernetics/von-foerster-1981
source @arxiv/algebra/peter-weyl-1927
source @arxiv/cybernetics/mead-1934

prism @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order {
  focus second_order
  project second_order
  split second_order
  shift second_order
  settle second_order
}

# === The observer carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming von Foerster's
# load-bearing primitive: the observer. The observer IS what reads an
# observation; at second-order altitude, the observer's reading IS
# itself an observation, subject to the same calculus.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref. Two observers
# with byte-equal underlying references ARE the same observer under
# the substrate's content-addressing.
type observer = ref

# === The observation carrier ===
#
# The act of an observer reading the world (or another observation).
# Per von Foerster, every observation IS an act by an observer; an
# observation without an observer is ill-formed; an observer without
# an observation has not yet drawn the distinction at altitude α.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type observation = ref

# === The observe operation ===
#
# Von Foerster's second-order primitive: observe takes an observer and
# an observation and returns the observation lifted to altitude α+1 —
# the observer's reading of the observation. Per the circular-
# reflexivity calculus, observe applied to the observation of an
# observer IS itself an observation; the recursion closes when observe
# lands on its own fixed point.
#
# The observe IS τ for Read A: the natural transition between observer
# and observation at the species boundary. See §8.7 Read A held via
# observer-of-observation at altitude α+1.
type observe_op = observer -> observation

# === The two value-level operations ===
#
# Read B held as load-bearing for epistemic novelty: first_order_state
# and second_order_state are the two verdicts the observer surfaces at
# any point within the observation-space. The verdict carrier IS the
# substrate's existing `verdict` family (success / partial / failure);
# the species realisation interprets the verdict per von Foerster's
# altitude-stratified semantics — first-order names the observation;
# second-order names the observer reading the observation.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary. Same shape
# as distinction.marked_state / unmarked_state and the four metalogue
# shims at `shards/code/metalogue.mirror`: the substrate declares the
# obligation; species bodies discharge when a consumer pulls.
first_order_state(o: observation) -> verdict { \ }
second_order_state(o: observation) -> verdict { \ }

# === The observe operator (von Foerster's second-order primitive) ===
#
# Applies the observer to an observation, returning the observation
# lifted to altitude α+1 — the reading the observer makes of the
# observation. The circular-reflexivity axiom (observation-of-an-
# observation IS an observation) is substrate-fact at the realisation
# boundary; the action body discharges per-species.
#
# Body shape: `\` per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]; the discharge IS
# the species-specific instantiation of von Foerster's primitive.
observe(obs: observer, o: observation) -> observation { \ }

# === The inheritance from eigenform ===
#
# Per §8.7 Q4 and §8.8.1: the observer-of-self fixed-point witness
# inherits from `eigenform` (recognition #38). One ancestor (eigenform),
# two inheritors (distinction at the floor, second_order at the
# ceiling). This shard declares the inheritance interface here:
# observer_of_self names the carrier the consumer threads through
# eigenform_witnessing without restating the fixed-point obligation
# at this altitude.
#
# The carrier's structure: seed = observer, iteration = observe over
# the observation-space, witness = the observer-of-self satisfying
# observer = observe(observer, observation(observer)). This IS the
# circular-reflexivity calculus lifted to eigenform's fixed_point
# carrier: the second-order observation lands at its fixed point when
# the observer reads itself reading itself.
#
# Returns `fixed_point<observer>`: the eigenform whose witness IS the
# observer that observes itself. Downstream consumers compose with
# eigenform_witnessing(carrier) to verify convergence; the body here
# threads the observer into the carrier per species realisation.
#
# This action IS the bridge the substrate uses to avoid restating
# fixed-point machinery at the second_order altitude. Per
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]: the fixed-point
# obligation already lives at eigenform; second_order names HOW the
# observer becomes the eigenform's witness via self-observation.
observer_of_self(obs: observer) -> fixed_point(observer) { \ }

# === second_order_well_formed — the bilateral verdict predicate ===
#
# `second_order_well_formed(carrier)` is the predicate consumer shards
# name in a `requires` clause to declare bilateral agreement (per
# recognition #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) that the
# (observer, observation) pair they hold IS a well-formed von Foerster
# second-order observation — i.e. observe satisfies the circular-
# reflexivity axiom (observation-of-an-observation IS an observation);
# the first_order_state and second_order_state verdicts partition the
# observation-space without remainder at adjacent altitudes.
#
# The bilateral commitment: the carrier commits to declaring the pair
# (observer, observation); the consumer commits to discharging the
# verification at the species boundary.
#
# Declared as a typed predicate so downstream species shards can write
# `requires second_order_well_formed(my_carrier)` — same shape as
# `variety.variety_preserving(species)`,
# `eigenform.eigenform_witnessing(carrier)`,
# `distinction.distinction_well_formed(carrier)`, and the metalogue
# `requires substrate_pull_preserving(shim_X)` pattern at
# `shards/code/metalogue.mirror`. The body is `\`; the discharge IS
# the conjunction of (circular-reflexivity axiom + verdict altitude-
# partition) at the species boundary.
#
# No `requires second_order_well_formed(…)` clauses are added at THIS
# shard: the property declares the predicate; consumers add the
# clauses when they pull. Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] the
# operational sibling at `@mirror/cybernetics/second_order` lands the
# same way.
second_order_well_formed(obs: observer, o: observation) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/cybernetic/second_order
out observer
out observation
out observe_op
out first_order_state
out second_order_state
out observe
out observer_of_self
out second_order_well_formed
